{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cat .pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation.md; git diff 319bfd9 d164153 -- pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go; cat .pose/rules/backend-go.md .pose/rules/documentation-style.md .pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cat .pose/specs/2026-11-16-pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation.md; git diff 319bfd9 d164153 -- pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go; cat .pose/rules/backend-go.md .pose/rules/documentation-style.md .pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md'","aggregated_output":"---\nslug: pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated_at: 2026-11-16\ncompleted_at:        # stamped on the transition to status: done\nsupersedes:          # slug of the superseded spec (when applicable)\ndepends_on:          # prerequisites, inline list: other-spec, milestone:<roadmap>/<id>, roadmap:<slug>\nremediates:          # optional explicit links: spec:slug@defect-fix, finding:rva-<16hex>/F1@revert (never inferred from depends_on)\npriority:            # integer >= 0 (lower = higher priority); ordering preference, not a blocker\ncomponents: pose-mcp\ntask_type: refactor\nsurface:             # optional: minimal | standard | full (default) — minimal drops Tasks and derivable report sections; `pose specs facts <slug>` derives them\ndelivers: capability:review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation\n---\n\n# Spec: pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation\n\n## 1. Intent\n\n### Goal\nFazer uma operação de read view ler, interpretar e conferir o ledger de revisão de cada projeto uma vez, e não a cada verificação de bundle que a operação faz.\n\n### Business value\nA primeira chamada `pose_closeout_state` de um servidor MCP no harne8 ainda leva de 140 a 200 s; a spec `pose-index-material-is-kept-per-repository-state` só acelerou as seguintes. O perfil de CPU de uma chamada mostra que cerca de 98 s vão para `federatedSourceProof`, que verifica o bundle de revisão de cada dependência federada. Numa só chamada, contada com uma build instrumentada sobre o harne8 com o pose-dist em 7e46b1e: 64 provas de fonte, 280 leituras de `ReadReviewRuns`, 304 de `ReadReviewAttestations`, 140 de `ReviewRoundOf` e 29.680 conferências de digest de transcript, sobre um ledger de 318 runs (80 MB de transcripts, 13 MB de attestations). SHA-256 sozinho soma 31 s de CPU, e cópia de memória e JSON somam outros 30 s. É o custo que deixa a primeira chamada acima dos tetos dos clientes do `conductor`.\n\n### Constraints\n- Dentro de uma operação a read view já devolve os mesmos bytes para a mesma leitura; o memo guarda só valores derivados dessas leituras e não pode mudar nenhuma resposta.\n- A primeira leitura de cada entrada continua passando pela read view, de modo que o fecho e a auditoria final da operação a cobrem.\n- O memo vive e morre com a operação; nada é guardado entre operações.\n\n### Non-goals\n- Mudar o formato do ledger, os limites de leitura ou o que uma verificação de bundle exige.\n- Guardar resultados entre operações (isso é da spec `pose-index-material-is-kept-per-repository-state`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Requirements\n\n### Functional\n- R1: Within a read-view operation, the engine shall read and parse a project's review runs, its review attestations per bundle filter, and each review bundle's header at most once, and shall answer every later request of that operation for them from the parsed result, filtered as before.\n- R2: Within a read-view operation, the engine shall check a transcript's digest at most once per transcript path, size and expected digest, and shall reuse the outcome.\n- R3: A store with no read-view operation shall read, parse and check as before, on every call.\n- R4: The answers of every review verification, closeout state and federated acceptance shall be the same with and without the memo, including when a record is lost, out of bound or unreadable.\n\n### Non-functional\n- No harne8, a CPU da primeira chamada `pose_closeout_state` de um servidor MCP cai para menos da metade, com o mesmo veredito; as conferências de transcript caem de 29.680 para no máximo o número de transcripts do ledger.\n\n### Security\n- Nenhuma mudança de autorização ou de limite: o memo guarda o que a operação já leu pelas raízes que ela autoriza.\n\n### Compatibility\n- Sem mudança de contrato, saída ou formato de arquivo.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Technical Plan\n\n### Affected areas\n- `pose/review_dispatch.go`: `ReadReviewRuns` e `reviewRunTranscriptIntact` passam pelo memo da operação.\n- `pose/review_bundle.go`: `ReadReviewAttestations` passa pelo memo da operação.\n- `pose/review_operation_view.go`: `readReviewBundleHeader` passa pelo memo da operação.\n- `pose/governance_read_view.go`: a operação carrega o memo, descartado com ela.\n\n### Artifacts\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_ledger_memo.go\n- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_ledger_memo_test.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\n- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go\n- modified: .pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\n- modified: .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json\n\n### Delivery targets\n\n- capability:review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/cmd/pose/main.go\n\nComposto em produção por toda operação de revisão, fechamento e aceitação federada que verifica bundles. Check permanente `review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation-integration`, evidenceClass `integration`, required: `go test ./internal/pose -run 'TestReviewLedgerIsReadOncePerOperation|TestReviewLedgerWithoutAnOperationIsReadEveryTime|TestReviewLedgerMemoAnswersAsAFreshRead' -count=1`.\n\n### API/contract changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Data/storage changes\n- Nenhuma.\n\n### Technical risks\n- Um chamador que altere o slice devolvido mudaria a resposta de chamadas seguintes; o memo devolve cópias.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Tasks\n\n### Implementation\n- [x] Memo de runs, attestations, cabeçalhos de bundle e conferência de transcript por operação (R1, R2, R3).\n- [x] Emenda D14 do ADR das leituras de governança.\n\n### Validation\n- [x] Testes de contagem e de equivalência das respostas, com prova de reprovação; medição no harne8.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Decisions\n\n### Decision D1\n- Date: 2026-11-16\n- Context: o perfil da primeira chamada mostrou o ledger do pose-dist lido 280 vezes e 29.680 conferências de transcript numa só operação; o maintainer escolheu um memo por operação.\n- Options considered: (a) memo por operação dos valores derivados do ledger; (b) guardar entre operações, junto do material do índice; (c) paralelizar as verificações.\n- Decision: (a).\n- Basis: R1, R2, R4\n- Rationale: dentro da operação a read view já fixa os bytes, então (a) não muda resposta nem fecho; (b) exigiria reproduzir o fecho do ledger a cada chamada; (c) foi medida no material do índice e não deu ganho (155 s contra cerca de 140 s).\n- Consequences: o custo do ledger passa a ser uma leitura por operação.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n### Strategy\nTestes que contam leituras e conferências numa operação e comparam as respostas com e sem memo; medição da primeira chamada MCP no harne8.\n\n### Deterministic checks\n\n#### Test\n- Command: `go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver ./internal/scaffold -count=1`\n- Scope: pose-mcp\n- Expected: verde\n\n### Execution log\n- Date: 2026-11-16\n- Environment: Linux, Go 1.26; clone limpo do harne8 em cc7780b1 com o pose-dist em 7e46b1e; `closeout-check spec:harne8-abm-governed-execution`, que equivale à primeira chamada de um servidor MCP.\n- Notes: sem o memo, 197 s de parede e 130 s de CPU; o ledger do pose-dist lido 280 vezes, attestations 304, 29.680 conferências de transcript. Com o memo de runs, attestations e transcripts, 3 leituras de runs, 46 de attestations, 212 conferências, 164 s e 92 s de CPU; o perfil passou a mostrar `ReadReviewBundles` lendo e hasheando os 1.724 bundles (104 MB) a cada chamada. Com o memo de cabeçalhos de bundle, 136 s e 53 s de CPU. O resto é Git: 8.960 comandos somando 94 s, dos quais 1.116 `git log -1 --format=%H -- <path>` (81 s) sobre 436 caminhos distintos. Com o commit-graph com filtros de Bloom de caminhos alterados (`git commit-graph write --reachable --changed-paths`) nos dois repositórios, cada uma dessas consultas cai de 47 ms para 2 ms, e duas chamadas MCP seguidas levam 59 s e 10 s, terminais. Sem o memo, o teste de contagem reprova (22 leituras de runs e 28 de cabeçalhos numa verificação da fixture); sem as cópias, o de equivalência reprova.\n\n### Results summary\n- Successes: a CPU da primeira chamada cai de 130 s para 53 s, com o mesmo veredito; com o commit-graph do Git, a primeira chamada leva 59 s.\n- Failures: nenhuma.\n- Warnings: sem o commit-graph, a parede da primeira chamada continua em cerca de 136 s, dominada por `git log -1 -- <path>`.\n\n### Requirement trace\n- R1 [satisfied] test:TestReviewLedgerIsReadOncePerOperation check:review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation-integration\n- R2 [satisfied] test:TestReviewLedgerIsReadOncePerOperation\n- R3 [satisfied] test:TestReviewLedgerWithoutAnOperationIsReadEveryTime\n- R4 [satisfied] test:TestReviewLedgerMemoAnswersAsAFreshRead\n\n### Known gaps\n- O ganho de parede da primeira chamada depende do commit-graph do Git, que é manutenção do repositório e não do motor (follow-up F1).\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Report\n\n### Delivered scope\n\nNão concluída.\n\n### Residual risks\n\n### Follow-ups\n\n- [open] F1: tornar o commit-graph com caminhos alterados parte da instalação e do CI: `pose update`/`pose doctor` reportam a falta dele e o comando que o escreve, e os workflows do harne8 e do pose-dist o escrevem antes dos gates; com ele, `git log -1 -- <path>` cai de 47 ms para 2 ms. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:high review:2026-11-23)\n- [open] F2: guardar entre operações as leituras Git puras do servidor MCP (o memo residente que o runtime de worktree já liga), para que os 1.116 `git log -1 -- <path>` de uma chamada, sobre 436 caminhos, não se repitam entre operações. (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:medium review:2026-11-23)\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\nindex d2da9242..e389a500 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\n@@ -3337,6 +3337,20 @@ type ReviewAttestationsRead struct {\n // names another bundle is not a loss for this one; one that names none is, because it may\n // be a rejection of this bundle.\n func (s Store) ReadReviewAttestations(bundleID string) (ReviewAttestationsRead, error) {\n+\tread, _, err := memoizedLedgerRead(s.fsys(), \"review-attestations\\x00\"+filepath.Clean(s.Root)+\"\\x00\"+bundleID, func() (ReviewAttestationsRead, error) {\n+\t\treturn s.readReviewAttestations(bundleID)\n+\t})\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn ReviewAttestationsRead{}, err\n+\t}\n+\tread.Attestations = append([]ReviewAttestation(nil), read.Attestations...)\n+\tread.Coverage.Losses = append([]SourceLoss(nil), read.Coverage.Losses...)\n+\treturn read, nil\n+}\n+\n+// readReviewAttestations reads the store's review attestations, those of\n+// bundleID when it is set, with the coverage of what could not be read.\n+func (s Store) readReviewAttestations(bundleID string) (ReviewAttestationsRead, error) {\n \tcoverage := SourceCoverage{Losses: []SourceLoss{}}\n \tdir, err := ensureReviewArtifactDirIn(s.fsys(), s.Root, filepath.ToSlash(filepath.Join(\".pose\", \"review-attestations\")), false)\n \tif os.IsNotExist(err) {\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\nindex 9d9e5442..2390a21c 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n@@ -247,6 +247,31 @@ func (s Store) ListReviewRuns(bundleID string) ([]ReviewRun, error) {\n }\n \n func (s Store) ReadReviewRuns(bundleID string) ([]ReviewRun, []string, error) {\n+\t// Within a read-view operation the ledger is read and checked once per\n+\t// root; every request of the operation is answered from that read,\n+\t// filtered by bundle as below (spec pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation).\n+\tall, _, err := memoizedLedgerRead(s.fsys(), \"review-runs\\x00\"+filepath.Clean(s.Root), func() (reviewRunsRead, error) {\n+\t\truns, lost, err := s.readAllReviewRuns()\n+\t\treturn reviewRunsRead{runs: runs, lost: lost}, err\n+\t})\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n+\t}\n+\tout := append([]ReviewRun(nil), all.runs...)\n+\tif bundleID != \"\" {\n+\t\tfiltered := []ReviewRun{}\n+\t\tfor _, run := range out {\n+\t\t\tif run.BundleID == bundleID {\n+\t\t\t\tfiltered = append(filtered, run)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tout = filtered\n+\t}\n+\treturn out, append([]string(nil), all.lost...), nil\n+}\n+\n+// readAllReviewRuns reads, checks and orders every review run of the store.\n+func (s Store) readAllReviewRuns() ([]ReviewRun, []string, error) {\n \tfiles := s.fsys()\n \tdir := filepath.Join(s.Root, filepath.FromSlash(reviewRunsDir))\n \t// The storage is read where the writer writes it: a link in its place is another place.\n@@ -361,15 +386,6 @@ func (s Store) ReadReviewRuns(bundleID string) ([]ReviewRun, []string, error) {\n \t}\n \tlost = append(lost, findings...)\n \tlost = append(lost, s.reviewContinuationFindings(out)...)\n-\tif bundleID != \"\" {\n-\t\tfiltered := []ReviewRun{}\n-\t\tfor _, run := range out {\n-\t\t\tif run.BundleID == bundleID {\n-\t\t\t\tfiltered = append(filtered, run)\n-\t\t\t}\n-\t\t}\n-\t\tout = filtered\n-\t}\n \treturn out, uniqueSorted(lost), nil\n }\n \n@@ -1642,6 +1658,15 @@ func validateReviewRunRecord(name string, run ReviewRun) error {\n const reviewTranscriptMaxBytes = 256 << 20\n \n func (s Store) reviewRunTranscriptIntact(run ReviewRun) string {\n+\tproblem, _, _ := memoizedLedgerRead(s.fsys(), \"transcript\\x00\"+filepath.Clean(s.Root)+\"\\x00\"+run.TranscriptPath+\"\\x00\"+run.TranscriptDigest, func() (string, error) {\n+\t\treturn s.checkReviewRunTranscript(run), nil\n+\t})\n+\treturn problem\n+}\n+\n+// checkReviewRunTranscript reads a run's transcript and checks it against\n+// the digest the run names; it returns the problem, or \"\".\n+func (s Store) checkReviewRunTranscript(run ReviewRun) string {\n \tfull := filepath.Join(s.Root, filepath.FromSlash(run.TranscriptPath))\n \tfiles := s.fsys()\n \tinfo, err := files.Lstat(full)\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\nindex 032c8a01..72133b77 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_operation_view.go\n@@ -24,6 +24,22 @@ type reviewHeaderObservation struct {\n // readReviewBundleHeader is the same classification for cached and live reads.\n // A known different owner is skippable only after whole-JSON and ambiguity checks.\n func readReviewBundleHeader(files Files, dir, name string) reviewHeaderObservation {\n+\t// A bundle's header is read, hashed and classified once per operation:\n+\t// a closeout lists every bundle for every scope it verifies (spec\n+\t// pose-review-ledger-is-read-once-per-operation).\n+\tobservation, _, _ := memoizedLedgerRead(files, \"bundle-header\\x00\"+filepath.Clean(dir)+\"\\x00\"+name, func() (reviewHeaderObservation, error) {\n+\t\treturn observeReviewBundleHeader(files, dir, name), nil\n+\t})\n+\tif observation.loss != nil {\n+\t\tloss := *observation.loss\n+\t\tobservation.loss = &loss\n+\t}\n+\treturn observation\n+}\n+\n+// observeReviewBundleHeader reads one bundle's bytes and classifies the scope\n+// they declare.\n+func observeReviewBundleHeader(files Files, dir, name string) reviewHeaderObservation {\n \trel := filepath.ToSlash(filepath.Join(\".pose\", \"review-bundles\", name))\n \traw, err := files.ReadFile(filepath.Join(dir, name))\n \tif err != nil {\n# Rule: Backend Go\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for HTTP handlers, domain services, persistence, concurrency, and integrations between Go services.\n\n## Required patterns\n\n- Handle and propagate errors with enough context for diagnosis.\n- Validate handler input and return HTTP status codes consistent with the contract.\n- Keep business rules in service or domain layers, not in transport code.\n- Honor `context.Context` for timeouts and cancellation.\n- Put data access behind clear interfaces that support testing.\n- Use structured logs without exposing sensitive data.\n\n## Blocking anti-patterns\n\n- Ignoring error returns, including `_` for critical errors.\n- Using `panic` in ordinary request flows instead of controlled error handling.\n- Coupling handlers directly to concrete repository implementations without an abstraction.\n- Running unbounded or unpaginated queries in potentially large endpoints.\n- Introducing concurrency without adequate synchronization or race protection.\n\n## Minimum checks\n\n- Run `go test ./...` in the affected scope.\n- Run `go test -race ./...` when concurrency changes.\n- Run `go vet ./...` without blocking findings.\n- Run the applicable Go lint check, such as `golangci-lint`, without critical errors.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n# Rule: Documentation Style\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide for process documentation, rules, specs, workflows, and operational instructions.\n\n## Required conventions\n\n- Write instructions in the imperative mood and begin them with action verbs.\n- Keep bullets short and limited to one idea.\n- Avoid duplicating sections with the same purpose across files.\n- Link to the single source of truth instead of copying its content.\n- Use `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` consistently.\n- State each instruction's scope explicitly to reduce ambiguity.\n\n## Examples: good and bad\n\n### Redundancy\n\n- **Good:** \"Update review criteria in `.pose/workflows/review.md` and reference that workflow from the root AGENTS file.\"\n- **Bad:** \"Repeat review criteria in AGENTS, the workflow, and every related spec.\"\n\n### Ambiguous reference\n\n- **Good:** \"Run the lint check described by the review workflow.\"\n- **Bad:** \"Run that standard validation before pushing.\"\n\n## Quick editorial checklist\n\n- Language is imperative and direct.\n- Bullets are short and non-overlapping.\n- Files do not duplicate sections.\n- `check`, `spec`, and `workflow` are used consistently.\n- References point to explicit files or paths.\n\n## Precedence in multi-domain conflicts\n\n- Apply the most restrictive security, contract, and operational rule when domain rules conflict.\n- Prefer verifiable check evidence and explicit risk mitigation when speed conflicts with control.\n- Record the precedence decision and objective rationale in the review.\n\n## Recurrence traceability\n\n> Also apply: [.pose/rules/_base-recurrence.md](_base-recurrence.md)\n# Rule: Knowledge Governance\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide when creating, updating, reviewing, or removing artifacts under `.pose/knowledge/`.\n\n## TTL and retention\n\n- Set `expires_at` on every artifact when it is created.\n- Use a default TTL of 30 days for notes, decision logs, and handoffs.\n- Use a TTL of up to 90 days only with a justification recorded in the artifact body.\n- Treat an artifact without `expires_at` as non-compliant and block its creation or merge.\n\n## When this is not the right home\n\n- Use `.pose/knowledge/` only for time-bound operational memory: content\n  tied to a decision moment, a handoff between executions, or something\n  meant to be reviewed and eventually expire.\n- A durable fact or convention that will not become false and carries no\n  review trigger — a third-party tool's parsing quirk, a naming\n  convention, a recurring gotcha — is not a `decision-log` just because no\n  better type exists. Route it to `.pose/rules/` instead: add it to an\n  existing rule file or create one, then wire it into the relevant task\n  type's base `rules` array in `.pose/indexes/task-map.json` so\n  `pose suggest <task>` surfaces it automatically. No path scoping is\n  required — a task type's base `rules` list is returned regardless of\n  `--path`; only language/component-specific rules need the\n  `rules_by_domain` layer.\n- Rule of thumb: if nothing was decided or traded off, and nothing about\n  the fact will change on a predictable timeline, it is not a\n  `decision-log` and not an ADR — it is a rule. See ADR\n  `2026-08-15-durable-non-architectural-knowledge-belongs-in-rules-not-a-new-type`.\n\n## Reusable cross-execution format\n\n- Structure reusable context as a handoff with fixed sections: Context, Current state, Next checks, Risks, and Next owner.\n- Keep `source_refs` linked to the relevant spec, workflow, and executed check commands.\n- Record `last_reviewed_at` in the body to make effective cross-execution updates traceable.\n\n## Archiving and purging\n\n- Run biweekly triage to list expired artifacts.\n- Move expired artifacts to `.pose/knowledge/archive/` when they retain audit value.\n- Purge archived artifacts 180 days after expiration unless documented legal or compliance requirements apply.\n- Record every archive and purge action in the housekeeping log.\n\n## Sensitive content\n\n- Prohibit secrets, tokens, credentials, private keys, and equivalent material.\n- Prohibit personal data and non-anonymized customer data.\n- Do not copy restricted incidents or reports in full; keep only a controlled reference.\n- Classify frontmatter `sensitivity` as `public-internal` or `restricted`.\n- Remove identified sensitive content immediately and open a security follow-up.\n\n## Ownership and review\n\n- Keep `@pose-maintainers` as the primary governance owner.\n- Require an owner in every artifact frontmatter.\n- Review expiration biweekly and quality monthly.\n- Escalate a backlog overdue by more than two cycles to the primary owner.\n- Block backlog growth when `list-expired` exceeds the operational limit: zero in strict mode, two in tolerant mode.\n\n## Minimum operational checks\n\n- Run `pose knowledge-check --strict` biweekly to validate the expired backlog.\n- Run `pose knowledge-housekeeping list-expired` for detailed triage.\n- Run `pose knowledge-housekeeping archive-expired --dry-run` before applying changes.\n- Execute destructive actions only with an explicit `--apply` flag.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
