{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'type .*Conclusion|type ReviewFinding|type ReviewToolDisposition|type ReviewCriterion struct' pose-mcp/internal/pose/{review_bundle.go,review_conclusions.go}; sed -n '1,90p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go; sed -n '330,386p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go; sed -n '130,146p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/source_coverage.go\"","aggregated_output":"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_conclusions.go:38:type ReviewConclusion struct {\npackage pose\n\n// Conclusions of delegated runs (spec pose-delegated-review-conclusions).\n//\n// A review run whose record is intact and signed, whose draft is complete\n// and valid for its round, and whose bundle still governs its scope is\n// turned by the engine into the attestation its draft concludes: the run's\n// proof is signed, the attestation is built from the draft's typed fields and\n// signed by the issuer the delegation policy names, and the domain writer\n// records it under the same preflight as every attestation (R1). Anything\n// short of that records no governed effect; the conclusion record of the run\n// says why (R3). One run concludes once: replaying it returns its record (R4).\n\nimport (\n\t\"encoding/json\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"time\"\n)\n\n// ReviewConclusionsDir holds one conclusion record per run.\nconst ReviewConclusionsDir = \".pose/review-conclusions\"\n\n// Conclusion states.\nconst (\n\tReviewConclusionRecorded = \"recorded\"\n\tReviewConclusionRefused  = \"refused\"\n\t// ReviewConclusionPending reserves a run while its conclusion is signed\n\t// and recorded.\n\tReviewConclusionPending = \"concluding\"\n)\n\n// ReviewConclusion is what the engine did with a run's conclusion.\ntype ReviewConclusion struct {\n\tSchemaVersion int    `json:\"schema_version\"`\n\tRunID         string `json:\"run_id\"`\n\tBundleID      string `json:\"bundle_id\"`\n\tScope         string `json:\"scope\"`\n\tState         string `json:\"state\"`\n\tDecision      string `json:\"decision,omitempty\"`\n\tAttestation   string `json:\"attestation,omitempty\"`\n\t// Kind is the run's kind and Destination where an adjudication or a smoke\n\t// verdict was recorded (spec pose-delegated-verdict-destinations).\n\tKind        string   `json:\"kind,omitempty\"`\n\tDestination string   `json:\"destination,omitempty\"`\n\tProofID     string   `json:\"proof_id,omitempty\"`\n\tIssuer      string   `json:\"issuer,omitempty\"`\n\tReasons     []string `json:\"reasons,omitempty\"`\n\tConcludedAt string   `json:\"concluded_at\"`\n\t// Replayed is set on a result that returns an earlier record (R4).\n\tReplayed bool `json:\"replayed,omitempty\"`\n}\n\nfunc reviewConclusionPath(root, runID string) string {\n\treturn filepath.Join(root, filepath.FromSlash(ReviewConclusionsDir), runID+\".json\")\n}\n\n// ReadReviewConclusion is the conclusion record of run, if any.\nfunc (s Store) ReadReviewConclusion(runID string) (*ReviewConclusion, error) {\n\tif !validAttemptFileName(runID) {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: %q is not a run id\", runID)\n\t}\n\tc, _, err := s.readReviewConclusionRaw(runID)\n\treturn c, err\n}\n\n// readReviewConclusionRaw is the conclusion record of run and the bytes it\n// was parsed from: one read, so what is judged is what a write expects\n// (review round 2, B4).\nfunc (s Store) readReviewConclusionRaw(runID string) (*ReviewConclusion, []byte, error) {\n\traw, err := readBoundedRegular(reviewConclusionPath(s.Root, runID), 1<<20)\n\tif errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\treturn nil, nil, nil\n\t}\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n\t}\n\tvar c ReviewConclusion\n\tif err := json.Unmarshal(raw, &c); err != nil || c.RunID != runID {\n\t\treturn nil, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: the conclusion record of %s cannot be read\", runID)\n\t}\n\treturn &c, raw, nil\n}\n\n// reviewConclusionChecks are the conditions a run must meet before its\n// conclusion is recorded, each a reason when it does not (R1, R3, R4).\n\t// attributed range spans — and that moves whenever anything else is\n\t// committed or reindexed. Sealing it would make an unrelated commit stale a\n\t// review of content that did not move, which is the invalidation rule this\n\t// contract exists to keep narrow. They are diagnostics, recomputed on every\n\t// preparation, like the warnings beside them.\n\tRangeObservations []ReviewBundleRangeObservation `json:\"range_observations,omitempty\"`\n\tWarnings          []string                       `json:\"warnings,omitempty\"`\n\tBlockers          []string                       `json:\"blockers,omitempty\"`\n\tPath              string                         `json:\"path,omitempty\"`\n}\n\ntype ReviewAttestationReuse struct {\n\tMode            string `json:\"mode,omitempty\"`\n\tCriterion       string `json:\"criterion\"`\n\tFromAttestation string `json:\"from_attestation\"`\n\tInputDigest     string `json:\"input_digest\"`\n}\n\ntype ReviewAttestationSignature struct {\n\tIssuer    string `json:\"issuer\"`\n\tSubject   string `json:\"subject\"`\n\tAlgorithm string `json:\"algorithm\"`\n\tPublicKey string `json:\"public_key\"`\n\tSignature string `json:\"signature\"`\n}\n\n// ReviewAuthorityClaim is what an authorized issuer asserts about who reviewed,\n// bound to the exact bundle they reviewed.\n//\n// The engine does not learn who anyone is from this. It verifies that an issuer\n// it trusts, holding the grant for the role being claimed, signed a statement\n// binding these principals and executions to this bundle — and that the\n// statement is current and addressed to this project. Whether the issuer told\n// the truth is the issuer's authority, not POSE's inference, and that boundary\n// is the honest one: the alternative is a local engine claiming to know\n// something no local evidence can show.\ntype ReviewAuthorityClaim struct {\n\tSchemaVersion int    `json:\"schema_version\"`\n\tProject       string `json:\"project\"`\n\tBundleDigest  string `json:\"bundle_digest\"`\n\t// Principal and Role describe the reviewer. Role is `agent` or `human`.\n\tPrincipal string `json:\"principal\"`\n\tRole      string `json:\"role\"`\n\t// ReviewExecution and ImplementationExecution are the two runs the\n\t// separation is about; ImplementationPrincipal is who produced the change.\n\tReviewExecution         string `json:\"review_execution\"`\n\tImplementationPrincipal string `json:\"implementation_principal\"`\n\tImplementationExecution string `json:\"implementation_execution\"`\n\tIssuer                  string `json:\"issuer\"`\n\tIssuedAt                string `json:\"issued_at\"`\n\tExpiresAt               string `json:\"expires_at,omitempty\"`\n\t// Audience is the project this claim was issued for. A claim replayed from\n\t// another project names that project here and stops being satisfied.\n\tAudience string `json:\"audience\"`\n}\n\ntype ReviewAttestation struct {\nfunc (c *SourceCoverage) Normalize() {\n\tif c.Losses == nil {\n\t\tc.Losses = []SourceLoss{}\n\t}\n\tsort.SliceStable(c.Exclusions, func(i, j int) bool { return c.Exclusions[i].Pattern < c.Exclusions[j].Pattern })\n\tsort.SliceStable(c.Losses, func(i, j int) bool {\n\t\ta, b := c.Losses[i], c.Losses[j]\n\t\tif a.Artifact != b.Artifact {\n\t\t\treturn a.Artifact < b.Artifact\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn a.Kind < b.Kind\n\t})\n}\n\n// Describe is a one-line account of the losses a read of scope has, for places that\n// carry text (a coverage detail, a limitation). It names no content: only where the\n// read failed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"The review will request changes for duplicate computation on concurrent misses and mutable nested data shared through the memo. I also found a smaller return-shape change: empty slices become nil, including for stores without an operation.\n\nThe sandbox rejected the restoration command, so the four generated assessment/state files remain modified. I have not changed implementation files or recorded an attestation."}}
